    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Well, Mitt Romney has always fascinated me as kind of a wild card in his political life as a moderate governor of Massachusetts, as a, quote, severely conservative presidential candidate in 2012. Then as a critic of Donald Trump, when Donald Trump took over the party, then as a potential Donald Trump cabinet member when he talked to him about being Secretary of State in 2016. Right. as a Senate candidate, someone who I wouldn't say embraced Donald Trump, but someone who certainly didn't push him away. And then as a Senator, someone who has been fairly unshy at times about defying Donald Trump, being critical of him.",
