    "turn_text": "And you take your oath seriously? I agree with most of the things the president has done, right? that policies he put in with regards to the economy are very close to the policies I campaigned on four years before. I agree with those things. The fact that economy is doing as well as it is is in part because of those policies. So he's going to take a bow for those policies. I'm with him. So I'm with the by the way, I think he's going to get reelected. I think if Bernie or Elizabeth is the nominee and the Democratic side, he'll get elected in a landslide. I will still vote for the policies I agree with. I'll stand in the plot when he says things that are wrong. But then he did one thing we know of was a very seriously wrong thing. And not to call it grievously wrong would be to violate my oath, violate my conscience, subject me to the censure of history. What kind of consequences do you think you'll I don't know what they'll be. There's some I know. I know they'll be in consequence. And I just have to recognize that and do what you think is right.",
